9. Preparing for EPA (STAR Method)

From page 16 :

STAR = Situation, Task, Action, Result

Applied Use

When answering questions:

Situation → context
Task → responsibility
Action → what YOU did
Result → outcome + learning
Example (Improved Answer)

Weak:

“I fixed a pipeline issue”

Strong:

“I identified a schema mismatch causing ingestion failure, implemented validation checks, and reduced data errors by 40%”

Instructor Insight

Results + learning = distinction-level answers

